OL,3,GNEWSACouncil pay-out for pregnant
OL,4,Awoman's 'unsafe' home
OL,5,
OL,6,FA council in west London has agreed to
OL,7,Fcompensate a woman #1,950 after it
OL,8,Fplaced her and her children in
OL,9,F"unsuitable" accommodation, while the
OL,10,Fwoman was pregnant.
OL,12,FThe woman, referred to as Miss D in a
OL,13,Freport on the case, approached
OL,14,FHillingdon Council in July 2024 for
OL,15,Fhomelessness assistance.
OL,17,FThe family were moved into emergency
OL,18,Faccommodation, and then into temporary
OL,19,Faccommodation for seven months, which
OL,20,Fthe woman described as having "exposed
OL,21,Fwiring, poor hygiene and unsafe
OL,22,Ffurniture".
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,325,320,200,140,0,100
